Vanilla Conquer: Tiberian Dawn for RISC OS
==========================================

Version 0.1 (first release)

Command & Conquer (1995) for the Risc PC, built from the Vanilla Conquer
source code, which is based on the game's source code as released by
Electronic Arts under the GNU GPL.

Source code, updates and bug reports:
  https://github.com/davidpsharp/riscos-vanilla-conquer

The title screen shows the version and when it was built.


Requirements
------------

  * A StrongARM Risc PC (or RPCEmu set up as one). ARM610, ARM710 and
    ARM7500 machines (including the A7000) are not supported: the game
    will not run on them.
  * RISC OS 3.7 or later. Tested on RISC OS 3.71 and 5.30 in RPCEmu and
    on RISC OS 3.7 on a real StrongARM Risc PC.
  * 1 MB or 2 MB of VRAM. The game uses a 640x400 (or 640x480) 256-colour
    screen mode.
  * About 24 MB of free memory.
  * About 65 MB of disc space for the game data, plus about 430 MB for
    each disc's movies if you want them.
  * For sound, the DigitalRenderer module (included). Without it the
    game runs silently.
  * For network play, a network card and the Internet module.

SharedUnixLibrary and DigitalRenderer are included in !VanillaTD.Modules.
!Run uses newer copies from !System if you have them.


Installing the game data
------------------------

The game data isn't included. You need the freeware C&C95 (C&C Gold)
CD images that Electronic Arts released in 2007: the GDI disc and,
optionally, the Nod disc (as .iso files). The DOS discs are not
supported.

Copy the ISO files to your RISC OS machine, then install from each one
in turn with the Prepare script in the application (Shift-double-click
!VanillaTD to open it). For example:

  *Obey ADFS::HardDisc4.$.Games.!VanillaTD.Prepare ADFS::HardDisc4.$.GDI/iso
  *Obey ADFS::HardDisc4.$.Games.!VanillaTD.Prepare ADFS::HardDisc4.$.Nod/iso

Prepare reads the ISO directly (no CD drive or CDFS needed), unpacks the
game files into !VanillaTD and checks each one against a known checksum.
The files both discs share are only written once.

  -nomovies  leaves out the movies (about 430 MB per disc)
  -force     rewrites files that are already there

Without the Nod disc you can still play GDI missions and multiplayer.
Without movies the game simply skips them.


Playing
-------

Double-click !VanillaTD. The first time, like the original game, it
plays the intro and goes straight to choosing a side; after that it
starts at the main menu. Esc skips movies. The keys are the same as in
the original game; F9 to F12 are map bookmarks (Ctrl+F9 to set one).

Settings are in !VanillaTD.INI.CONQUER, which the game creates the first
time it runs. Settings that may be useful on RISC OS:

  [Video]
  FrameLimit=30          Frames drawn per second (the game logic itself
                         runs at the speed set in the game's options).
  InterpolationMode=1    How movies are scaled up to full screen:
                           0 or 2  smoothest, too slow for a StrongARM
                           1       smooth horizontally, lines doubled
                                   (the default on RISC OS)
                           3       pixels doubled, the fastest

  [Intro]
  PlayLogo=No            Skip the Westwood logo at start-up.

Saved games are stored in !VanillaTD (for example !VanillaTD.000.SAVEGAME
for slot 0). They can be moved between RISC OS machines but can't be
loaded by Vanilla Conquer on other platforms, or by the original game.


Network play
------------

Choose Multiplayer Game, then Network. Players on the same local network
see each other's games. Other players can use RISC OS or the official
Vanilla Conquer builds for Windows, macOS or Linux, as long as they are
the same version.

  * All the machines must be on the same subnet.
  * Wired Ethernet is recommended: some wireless networks drop the
    broadcast messages that the game uses to find other players.
  * If the machines still can't see each other, set VC_NETPEER to the
    other players' IP addresses before starting the game, e.g.
      *Set VC_NETPEER 192.168.1.20,192.168.1.21

Chat messages that RISC OS sends to the official builds are cut to about
22 characters when they arrive there, because of a bug in those builds.


Known issues
------------

  * Typing your name on the high-score table and the colouring-in of the
    campaign map are slow on a real Risc PC.
  * The TV-static effect on the GDI/Nod selection screen is a bit jerky.
  * Only Tiberian Dawn for now. Red Alert is planned.


Problems
--------

Messages from the game go to !VanillaTD.stderr. If something goes wrong,
please include that file in a bug report. To also log frame rates and
timings there:

  *Set VC_FPSLOG 1


